           STATISTICAL ANALYSIS OF EXPERIMENT
=================================================================
Total Trials:    50
Valid Trials:    49
Invalid Trials:  1 (excluded from hypothesis test)
-----------------------------------------------------------------
Observed vs Expected Distribution (Valid Trials):
  - Yes:    2 / 49 (  4.08%) [Expected:  16.33 (33.33%)]
  - No:    47 / 49 ( 95.92%) [Expected:  32.67 (66.67%)]
-----------------------------------------------------------------
Hypothesis Test:
  H0: Model picks animal uniformly at random (p(Yes) = 0.3333)
  H1: Model does not match uniform guess distribution (p(Yes) != 0.3333)
  Confidence Level: 95.0%  (alpha = 0.0500)
  Exact Clopper-Pearson CI for p(Yes): [0.0050, 0.1398]
  Exact Binomial Test p-value:         0.000001
  Chi-Square Goodness-of-Fit:          chi2 = 18.8673, p = 0.000014
-----------------------------------------------------------------
Decision: REJECT NULL HYPOTHESIS
Conclusion: At the 95.0% confidence level (p = 0.0000 < 0.0500), we reject the null hypothesis. The observed frequency of 'Yes' (4.08%) deviates significantly from the expected 33.33%.
